---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../data/site";
import { legal } from "../data/content";
---

<LegalPage
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  title="Your day is yours."
  description="How Jamaal and this website handle your information."
  updated={legal.updated}
>
  <h2 id="short-version">The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Jamaal is made by fhdamd (Fahad Ahmed) in Melbourne, Australia. The app keeps your tasks, habits and Anchors on
    your device and, if you choose to sync, in your own iCloud. We don't receive them. This website collects what you
    give it when you join the early-access list and, only if you accept, counts visits with Google Analytics.
  </p>

  <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
  <p>
    Jamaal has a single Today list. You create Tasks, Habits and Anchors, they appear on Today, and you plan tomorrow at
    the right time. Everything you create, and your Wellbeing reading, is stored on your device. If you turn on sync, it
    is stored in your own iCloud account, using Apple's services, under your Apple ID. fhdamd doesn't receive, read or
    store it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are sold and billed by Apple. We don't see your payment details; Apple tells us only whether a
    subscription is active.
  </p>

  <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics, through our Firebase project, to count visits to this website: which pages are viewed,
    roughly where visitors come from, and what kind of device and browser they use. It sets cookies (<code>_ga</code>
    and <code>_ga_</code> followed by an identifier, which last up to two years), so it only loads if you choose Accept
    in the banner. If you choose Decline, the site works the same and nothing is set. You can change your choice at any
    time with "Cookie settings" in the footer; declining later also removes the cookies we set.
  </p>
  <p>
    We turn off Google signals and ad personalisation, we don't use this data for advertising, and we keep it for the
    shortest period Google offers. The Jamaal app collects no analytics at all.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Google Firebase Hosting, which keeps standard server logs (such as IP address and the pages
    requested) to run and secure the service. There are no other trackers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="list">The early-access list</h2>
  <p>If you join the list, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your first name and email address, so we can write to you;</li>
    <li>once the TestFlight beta is open, which devices you plan to test on (iPhone, iPad or Mac);</li>
    <li>which form you used on the site, and when you joined.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use them to email you when Jamaal is ready, when a TestFlight beta opens, and to send your beta invitation. We
    don't send anything else, and we don't sell or share your details or use them for advertising.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the beta opens, we add the name and email you gave us to TestFlight through Apple's App Store Connect so Apple
    can email you the invitation. Apple handles them under its own privacy policy. Any email we send is sent through an
    email service provider that handles it on our behalf.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your details are stored with Google Firebase (Cloud Firestore), in the United States, which processes them on our
    behalf. We keep them while the list is open and until you ask us to remove them.
  </p>
  <p>
    To stop the form being abused, the signup service counts attempts from each network address. It keeps only a one-way
    hash of the address, never the address itself, and deletes it automatically within a day.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct or delete what we hold about you at any time by emailing{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. We'll reply and act on it promptly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top. If a change affects the early-access list,
    we'll tell the people on it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
